// Band of the Week Website + Merch comp.
//
// DO NOT replace the live Firestore rules with this file.
// DO NOT deploy hosting, functions, or rules from this snippet.
// Publish rules only, as a separate manual step, after editing the live ruleset in place.
//
// The comp document is the only record the website trusts. Admin SDK writes it.
// Clients must not be able to create, extend, or revoke it.
//
// Firestore allows a request if ANY matching allow rule allows it.
// Earlier notes in this repo say the live rules end in a catch-all deny.
// Confirm that is still true before publishing. A wildcard allow-write would
// override the write deny below, and this prize would not be server-trusted.

match /botwWebsiteComps/{profileId} {
  // Public read: the band website and merch pages decide access from this date.
  // The document stores an end date, a reason, and admin ids. No payment data.
  allow read: if true;
  allow create, update, delete: if false;
}

// The grant function also writes these marker fields on merchStores/{id} and
// merchStorefronts/{id}: botwCompExpiresOn, botwCompRevoked.
// Cloud Functions bypass rules. If a band or musician can already update those
// documents, add this helper and require it on their update rule so they cannot
// extend the prize. Leave the administrator update path able to change them.
//
// function botwCompMarkersUnchanged() {
//   return !request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys()
//     .hasAny(['botwCompExpiresOn', 'botwCompRevoked']);
// }
//
// allow update: if isOwner() && botwCompMarkersUnchanged();
//
// If only isAdmin() can write merchStores and merchStorefronts, no further
// edit is required. Do not put the prize end date on the profile document;
// profile saves are client merges and are not the source of truth.
